#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124219 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "4c1e01c1-d607-5ad8-8643-b3317201ab9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4832" :question/problem "Let $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2\\}$ and $\\mathcal{C}=\\{\\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2\\}$ be bases of $\\mathbb{R}^2$. If $\\mathbf{c}_1=\\mathbf{b}_2-4\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{c}_2=5\\mathbf{b}_1+7\\mathbf{b}_2$, find the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small\\mathcal{C}\\to\\mathcal{B}}$ from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$." :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $\\mathcal{C}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ are\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $\\mathcal{C}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124220 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "93b466b2-9b8d-55fa-87b8-b5bf24a497cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-4833" :question/problem "Let $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2,\\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ be a basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and let $\\mathcal{S}$ be the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$. Find the values of $a,b$, and $c$ if\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{S}$ is\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & a & 2 \\\\ -3 & 7 & b \\\\ c & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ consists of the vectors $\\mathbf e_1, \\mathbf e_2$, and $\\mathbf e_3$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{S}$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{S}$.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, $a=0$, $b=0$, and $c=10$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124221 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6c5b5534-2082-593e-af07-df83497ea84c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4835" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$. Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of $P_{\\small\\mathcal{B}\\to\\mathcal{C}}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{C → B} &= P_{B → C}^{-1} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}^{-1} \\\\\n&= (1)/((-4) \\cdot 5 - (-6) \\cdot 3)\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} & -3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124222 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Between Two Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "0929855b-0310-5c87-8cff-cc2faa8a5ae0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4837" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ be bases of $\\mathbb{R}^2$. Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ as $\\{\\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ and $\\{\\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$.\n\nSo, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$. We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n$\\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid; c_{1}\\begin{vmatrix}c_{2} & b_{1}\\end{vmatrix}b_{2}; \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{bmatrix} & R_{1}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nP_{B → C} = \\mid \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 22 \\\\ 1 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802c32d5-200e-57b5-b136-227740e3bfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122009} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4e381e-da75-5e74-9e9c-a3391a5c5f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122010} {:answer/id #uuid "472db7aa-9e2f-5042-a922-3dba61445603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122011} {:answer/id #uuid "49e2de5a-38c3-55b3-8e74-a4de4b4ca09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122012} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3f0a84-127b-57de-a732-c93d89d954ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b3f0a84-127b-57de-a732-c93d89d954ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122013} :answer-field/id #uuid "687b3ca8-e3d6-5649-8e48-2f44b3197bae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122008}] :question/id #uuid "51bd98dc-1e1e-5c5c-9609-7609b0be859e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35799" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n\n$P_{C → B} = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "918ee8b8-0471-5b56-9d4a-d1bea72a1798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122369} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fa9047-f7e8-5f9d-9949-d7729255d727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122370} {:answer/id #uuid "137fcdf5-5430-5185-9456-e37560c66253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122371} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9c852b-8ae9-5e00-8520-24a9937f102d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122372} {:answer/id #uuid "5849b7d5-8611-5d5c-9543-42b26d93c84b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137fcdf5-5430-5185-9456-e37560c66253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122371} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99babbf-598a-548e-8170-a53c9365a613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122368}] :question/id #uuid "b7561091-5a13-5f20-989c-89982f4b4b54" :question/math-academy-id "q-36366" :question/problem "Let $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}}$ be a basis of $R^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of $R^{2}$.\n\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{B → S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if\n$b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf68c62-28b3-5d9f-9652-c3758a16a9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a =-5$, $b = 4$, and $c = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122405} {:answer/id #uuid "307a9f6d-ee4c-5d57-ad4c-17f2f1968898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a =-3$, $b =-1$, and $c = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122406} {:answer/id #uuid "3b60303c-9812-55b1-9ca2-ef4051d54dbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a =-3$, $b = 0$, and $c = 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122407} {:answer/id #uuid "5b976382-99d9-5e00-80d8-763c8680331e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a =-3$, $b = 0$, and $c = 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122408} {:answer/id #uuid "5dddeb41-19c3-5714-a541-71aa5c68021e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 0$, $b = 0$, and $c = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307a9f6d-ee4c-5d57-ad4c-17f2f1968898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a =-3$, $b =-1$, and $c = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122406} :answer-field/id #uuid "1638195c-a2ae-5016-b49e-560137dfa442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122404}] :question/id #uuid "62a8923e-9667-58a1-b193-1a3c8d5a2238" :question/math-academy-id "q-36400" :question/problem "Let $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}$ be a basis of $R^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of $R^{3}$. What are the values of $a, b$, and $c$ if\n\n$b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, b_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$P_{B → S} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e770330-d537-55a0-b76d-c5bc62cb87f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 2$, $b = 0$, and $c =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123887} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4463d0-6fb2-5c09-ab26-2ee0ecc2f580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 1$, $b = 2$, and $c = 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123888} {:answer/id #uuid "49c33f39-b355-525f-a670-ec0e685d82f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 0$, $b = 2$, and $c =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123889} {:answer/id #uuid "66dbad2c-55ba-55e6-8064-47ba319ac4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 2$, $b = 2$, and $c = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123890} {:answer/id #uuid "7b16e7ab-531f-50f7-a1ed-2e45be80bd6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 1$, $b =-2$, and $c = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66dbad2c-55ba-55e6-8064-47ba319ac4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a = 2$, $b = 2$, and $c = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123890} :answer-field/id #uuid "06119f1c-652a-522c-8b2e-b565ba854ca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123886}] :question/id #uuid "8ff70514-6088-5578-a352-2d83d0571687" :question/math-academy-id "q-81394" :question/problem "Let $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}$ and $C = {c_{1}, c_{2}, c_{3}}$ be bases of $R^{3}$.\nWhat are the values of $a, b$, and $c$ if\n\n$b_{1}|= c_{1} + 2c_{2} - c_{3},; b_{2}|= 5c_{3} + 2c_{2},; b_{3}|= c_{2} - c_{1}$,\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$P_{B → C} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ a & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & c & 0\\end{bmatrix}$?"}]}
